  partName: Intake Valve
  description: The Intake Valve is a tiny, elongated component located at the top-center-front
    of the engine, made of Material.001, responsible for controlling the flow of
    air and fuel into the combustion chamber. Its precise operation is crucial, as
    it enables the engine to draw in the optimal amount of air and fuel, and a notable
    aspect is that it is designed to open and close rapidly, typically in a matter
    of milliseconds. The intake valve's tiny size and elongated shape allow it to
    fit within the engine's compact cylinder head.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
